Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:20:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ink_detection: threshold, pick the binarization threshold
 from labelled predictions

`calibrate` finds the F1-optimal threshold of each labelled prediction made by
one checkpoint and stores their median; with two or more scrolls it scores each
scroll at the other scrolls' median and at 128, so the cost of each choice is
visible before reading an unlabelled scroll. `apply` binarizes at that value.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
